1. Title
Cuckoo Search via Lévy Flights

2. Authors
Xin-She Yang – Department of Engineering, University of Cambridge, UK.

Suash Deb – Department of Computer Science and Engineering, C. V. Raman College of Engineering, India.

Publication: World Congress on Nature & Biologically Inspired Computing (NaBIC 2009), December 2009.

arXiv+1
3. Problem Statement
The main problem addressed in this paper is to develop an efficient nature-inspired optimization algorithm called Cuckoo Search (CS) to solve optimization problems.

Traditional optimization algorithms may face difficulties in finding global optimal solutions, especially for complex optimization problems.

The paper proposes an algorithm based on:

The brood parasitic behaviour of cuckoo birds.

Lévy flight behaviour of some birds and fruit flies.

The selection of the best solutions.

Abandoning poor solutions and generating new solutions.

The objective is to improve optimization performance by finding better solutions efficiently.

The proposed algorithm is tested using benchmark functions and its performance is compared with Genetic Algorithm (GA) and Particle Swarm Optimization (PSO).

